From: Krzysztof Drobiński <krzysztof@kd-solutions.pl>
Subject: [PATCH] bindings: restrict the file allowlist to Ruby header directories

Matching "ruby" anywhere in a header path includes every system header
when the build directory itself contains "ruby", as with the
ruby-gem-commonmarker recipe. In particular, math.h contributes both
macros and enum variants for FP_* constants, producing duplicate Rust
definitions.

Match the ruby or ruby-VERSION directory component instead. This keeps
Ruby headers and their recursively required types without admitting
unrelated headers based on the name of a parent build directory.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/bindings.rs
+++ b/src/bindings.rs
@@ -62,7 +62,7 @@ pub fn generate(
     }
 
     let bindings = default_bindgen(clang_args, rbconfig)
-        .allowlist_file(".*ruby.*")
+        .allowlist_file(r".*[\\/]ruby(?:-[0-9][^\\/]*)?[\\/].*")
         .blocklist_item("ruby_abi_version")
         .blocklist_function("rb_tr_abi_version")
         .blocklist_function("^__.*")
